@claude

# UBERBOND NIGHTFALL SINGULARITY EXPANSION
## DO NOT STOP WHEN THE SCHEDULER WORKS

This is an expansion of the existing NIGHTFALL SUPREME mission. Treat the original issue body as Wave 0. This directive describes the destination after basic cloud liveness exists.

The owner does not want a patched SaaS. The owner wants UberBond to become an unusually capable, globally runnable, founder-light economic operating system that can continuously discover, evaluate, assemble, distribute, sell, fulfill, reconcile, learn, upgrade and redeploy lawful commercial systems from one shared core.

The wealth ambition is extreme. Treat it as an optimization direction, never as a guarantee and never as permission to fake revenue, demand, users or provider evidence.

Do not finish after one PR. Do not finish after one deployment. Do not finish after one offer. Do not finish after one integration. Continue until the repository-wide internal frontier contains no material dependency-satisfied build gap whose expected leverage exceeds its maintenance/risk burden.

# SINGULARITY LAW

UberBond should behave increasingly like a company compiler:

`world signals -> opportunity graph -> mechanism graph -> evidence -> economics -> offer compiler -> target/account graph -> distribution allocator -> sales state -> payment -> delivery compiler -> acceptance -> retention/renewal -> contribution economics -> learning -> capital/attention allocation -> capability acquisition -> code change -> verification -> deployment -> repeat`

Every edge needs explicit truth semantics. No state may invent the next state.

# A. RECONCILE THE ENTIRE UBERBOND UNIVERSE

Before building new abstractions, mine repository canon, historical lineage, current modules, closed/open PRs/issues, donor docs and retained artifacts for all named systems/features worth preserving. Build a durable machine-readable project graph that distinguishes:

- CURRENT_CANON
- CURRENT_PROGRAM
- INTERNAL_CAPABILITY
- PROVIDER_ADAPTER
- EXTERNAL_PROOF_REQUIRED
- HISTORICAL_DONOR
- SUPERSEDED
- REJECTED
- FROZEN
- OWNER_RECALLED_UNRESOLVED

Recover and link, where substantiated:

- OMNIA generations and V9 admission kernel;
- Prometheus;
- Cognitive Bus;
- Kilimanjaro;
- Everest;
- SUMMIT 100;
- BLACK SKY;
- Reality Activation;
- World Distribution OS;
- Total Commercial Genome / Wealth Engine;
- Proven Business Genome / Combination Engine;
- Total AI Revenue Frontier;
- First-Cash / First-Revenue systems;
- Offline Revenue Factory;
- Demand Recovery Assurance;
- Lead OS / Apollo-style targeting;
- Instantly-style outbound;
- Automation Capability Acquisition Frontier;
- Brain / cross-chat continuity;
- all six strategic product families;
- recurring-product ladder;
- long-term platform ladder;
- partner-gated offer lineage;
- hundreds of historical opportunity/offer records and thousands of scored combinations.

Do not flatten historical breadth into the latest commercial wedge.

# B. MERGE / RECONCILE EVERYTHING WORTH KEEPING

Search branches, PRs, closed PRs, recent commits, archived/donor directories and duplicate implementations.

For every non-main implementation classify:

- ALREADY_ABSORBED
- STRONGER_THAN_MAIN
- PARTIALLY_USEFUL
- CONFLICTING
- OBSOLETE
- UNSAFE
- DOCS_ONLY
- TEST_DONOR

Then:

- merge/cherry-pick verified stronger work;
- port useful tests/invariants when source code is obsolete;
- port useful capability slices when architecture is compatible;
- close superseded PRs with receipts;
- delete accidental duplicate architecture only when safe and clearly redundant;
- never blindly merge stale branches wholesale;
- never merge code because its branch name sounds ambitious;
- preserve provenance of absorbed donor work.

Goal: no valuable feature remains marooned on an old branch merely because the project history is huge.

# C. CAPABILITY ATOM LIBRARY

Represent UberBond as reusable economic capability atoms, not products welded together.

Capability families should cover at least:

## Intelligence
- public-source discovery;
- market-signal ingestion;
- opportunity detection;
- competitor/product intelligence;
- vertical intelligence;
- pricing intelligence;
- buyer-trigger detection;
- account research;
- public-contact provenance;
- mechanism extraction;
- evidence freshness;
- contradiction handling;
- structured research receipts.

## Targeting / enrichment
- account graph;
- ICP definitions;
- personas;
- saved searches;
- segmentation;
- intent signals where lawfully available;
- technology/company attributes;
- public-contact provenance;
- hygiene;
- suppression;
- enrichment waterfalls;
- dedupe;
- confidence;
- provenance.

Never infer private contact data merely to increase volume.

## Distribution
- partner/agency/MSP/reseller;
- direct email;
- inbound forms;
- web diagnostics;
- SEO;
- AEO;
- social;
- content;
- directory/marketplace;
- communities;
- referrals;
- affiliates;
- embedded/API/MCP distribution;
- reactivation;
- customer expansion;
- voice/SMS where authorized;
- paid media gated by economics/spend authority.

## Sales / conversion
- reply classification;
- lead qualification;
- routing;
- appointment booking;
- meeting prep;
- call state;
- discovery-question systems;
- objection library;
- proposal generation;
- quote lifecycle;
- pricing/scoping;
- commercial document lifecycle;
- signature;
- checkout/invoice preparation;
- pipeline state;
- loss reasons.

## Fulfilment
- scope compiler;
- workflow compiler;
- browser automation;
- API/tool execution;
- evidence collection;
- QA;
- human review gates;
- acceptance criteria;
- artifact packaging;
- delivery receipt;
- exception queue;
- repair/retest;
- SLA/monitoring.

## Customer success
- onboarding;
- health;
- monitoring;
- support;
- incident management;
- feedback;
- review requests where authorized;
- usage/value reporting;
- renewal triggers;
- expansion triggers;
- referral triggers;
- churn reasons;
- win-back/reactivation.

## Money / economics
- invoice/receivables;
- cleared-payment evidence;
- payment reconciliation;
- refunds;
- disputes;
- reversals;
- renewal payment;
- contribution margin;
- direct cost allocation;
- founder-minute accounting;
- partner commissions;
- referral attribution;
- accounting export;
- runway/capital allocation;
- unit-economics scenarios.

## Company operations
- task/mission graph;
- scheduler;
- provider health;
- dead letters;
- audit;
- secret boundaries;
- policy/authority;
- observability;
- deployment;
- rollback;
- continuity;
- owner-action queue;
- incident response;
- self-upgrade frontier.

Every new capability gets a canonical ID, inputs, outputs, evidence class, authority requirement, effects, provider options, cost model, failure semantics, retry semantics, tests and reusable offer links.

# D. BUSINESS MECHANISM GRAPH

Rebuild the useful Commercial Genome concept as executable structured state.

Mechanisms should include patterns such as:

- recovery of lost demand;
- reconciliation;
- compliance/evidence production;
- monitoring;
- exception management;
- white-label fulfilment;
- partner distribution;
- recurring monitoring;
- transaction assurance;
- revenue leakage detection;
- acceptance testing;
- quality assurance;
- marketplace matching;
- benchmarking;
- workflow automation;
- retention/reactivation;
- referral loops;
- data/evidence network effects;
- usage-based economics;
- API/embedded distribution;
- service-to-software progression.

Each mechanism must map to:

`buyer pain -> value mechanism -> capability atoms -> evidence required -> distribution fit -> recurring trigger -> costs -> risks -> proof state`

# E. OPPORTUNITY ENGINE V2

Build a continuously reusable opportunity engine, not an idea generator.

Ingest:

- current public web signals;
- official vendor/platform changes;
- product launches;
- pricing changes;
- regulatory/standards changes;
- recurring buyer complaints;
- job-posting demand signals;
- public procurement/RFP patterns where lawful;
- software gaps;
- workflow pain;
- community discussion;
- market saturation;
- new API/model capabilities;
- internal delivery capabilities;
- current provider costs;
- historical UberBond research.

Every opportunity gets:

- immutable ID;
- source/evidence set;
- observedAt;
- buyer;
- urgency;
- current alternative;
- expected value mechanism;
- delivery complexity;
- required capabilities;
- missing capabilities;
- provider dependencies;
- distribution accessibility;
- partner leverage;
- recurring trigger;
- gross-margin hypothesis;
- support burden;
- founder-minute estimate;
- payment friction;
- geography/legal constraints;
- downside;
- confidence;
- falsification condition;
- state.

Tournament score should optimize risk-adjusted contribution/founder-minute and first-proof speed, with diversity/concentration constraints.

# F. OFFER COMPILER / PRODUCT GENOME

Build one canonical ServiceSKU / ProductSKU compiler.

Input:

- opportunity;
- buyer;
- capability graph;
- distribution channel;
- desired result;
- constraints;
- provider availability;
- evidence/authority requirements.

Output:

- offer identity;
- positioning;
- scope;
- exclusions;
- delivery protocol;
- SLA;
- acceptance tests;
- required customer inputs;
- evidence plan;
- pricing models;
- direct-cost estimate;
- founder-minute budget;
- support model;
- guarantee/no-guarantee language;
- payment terms;
- renewal/expansion path;
- upsells/cross-sells;
- distribution-ready assets;
- kill criteria.

Support:

- one-off services;
- recurring managed services;
- diagnostics;
- monitoring products;
- white-label backend services;
- partner plans;
- usage-based API products;
- embedded products;
- evidence/reporting products;
- eventually self-serve SaaS only after repeated paid demand.

Do not build full SaaS before evidence earns it.

# G. DISTRIBUTION SINGULARITY

Make distribution a first-class adaptive portfolio allocator.

Required channel classes:

### Partner distribution
- agencies;
- MSPs;
- consultants;
- implementation partners;
- accountants/compliance providers where relevant;
- vertical software consultants;
- resellers;
- affiliates;
- referral partners;
- white-label delivery.

Build partner profiles, eligibility, capabilities, territories, downstream account models, commission/revenue-share schemas, partner attribution, conflicts, enablement assets and partner performance economics.

### Direct outbound
Reuse existing Instantly-style engine.

Extend only missing leverage:
- Apollo-style target builder;
- lawful/public-source enrichment;
- persona/search views;
- Clay-style enrichment waterfall patterns;
- hygiene;
- intent prioritization;
- account scoring;
- reply/meeting pipeline;
- sequence experiments;
- deliverability budget;
- domain/mailbox reputation isolation;
- channel-level contribution attribution.

### Product-led acquisition
Build reusable mini-tools/diagnostics that can generate useful proof before a sales call:
- scanners;
- calculators;
- evidence snapshots;
- benchmark reports;
- QA checks;
- health checks;
- gap audits;
- preview reports.

They must be low-cost, evidence-based and tied to canonical opportunities/offers.

### Owned content / SEO / AEO
Create capability for:
- programmatic but quality-gated landing pages;
- comparison pages;
- problem/solution pages;
- evidence-backed guides;
- structured data;
- FAQ/schema;
- indexation manifests;
- internal linking;
- content refresh;
- topical clusters;
- answer-engine-friendly summaries;
- content attribution to leads/payment.

No spam farms or scraped plagiarism.

### Social
Use the existing social-publication contract to compose scheduled content pipelines, repurposing, proof snippets, educational posts, case-study templates and launch/update assets. No live publishing without the consequence gate.

### Marketplaces / directories / ecosystems
Maintain opportunity surfaces for marketplaces, integrations, partner directories, app stores and ecosystem listings where appropriate. Prepare assets, schemas and eligibility state; do not submit without authority.

### API / MCP / agent distribution
Build product surfaces that other agents/software can invoke:
- diagnostics;
- research;
- evidence retrieval;
- offer configuration;
- reporting;
- monitoring;
- partner fulfilment.

Use explicit auth, quotas, usage/economics, tenant separation and consequence boundaries.

# H. SALES OPERATING SYSTEM

Unify all channels into one sales state machine.

States should support:

- unknown;
- researched;
- eligible;
- contacted/attributed;
- engaged;
- qualified;
- discovery;
- proposal;
- commercial review;
- awaiting payment;
- paid;
- delivery;
- acceptance;
- active;
- renewal;
- expanded;
- churned;
- disqualified;
- suppressed;
- uncertain external state.

No channel-specific duplicate customer truth.

Build:
- account timeline;
- attribution;
- objections;
- next-best action;
- stage transition requirements;
- SLA timers;
- owner escalation;
- no-response and reactivation rules;
- partner attribution;
- canonical loss reasons.

# I. DELIVERY COMPILER

For each paid ServiceSKU compile a delivery run from reusable capabilities.

Features:

- immutable paid scope;
- customer-input requirements;
- prerequisites;
- deterministic workflow first;
- AI/tool steps only where justified;
- provider selection;
- cost ceilings;
- time ceilings;
- quality tests;
- evidence bundle;
- acceptance artifact;
- retry/repair policy;
- human escalation;
- final receipt;
- recurring monitor creation.

Build reusable delivery templates across strategic families rather than bespoke scripts per customer.

# J. CUSTOMER SUCCESS / RETENTION ENGINE

Create a canonical post-delivery engine:

`accepted delivery -> monitoring -> measurable value -> health -> issue detection -> recovery -> renewal trigger -> expansion/referral`

Capabilities:
- onboarding checklists;
- customer health;
- value/evidence reports;
- monitoring alerts;
- SLA exception handling;
- feedback ingestion;
- satisfaction/acceptance distinction;
- renewal calendar;
- renewal evidence;
- expansion recommendations;
- cross-offer recommendations;
- referral eligibility;
- churn prediction only as probabilistic signal;
- win-back plans.

Retention models may prioritize work but cannot invent renewal truth.

# K. FINANCE / ECONOMIC BRAIN

Build one contribution-profit truth layer.

Track:
- cleared revenue;
- refunds;
- disputes;
- reversals;
- provider spend;
- model spend;
- telephony/SMS/email spend;
- delivery costs;
- incremental support costs;
- partner commissions;
- variable acquisition cost;
- founder minutes;
- payment timing;
- retention/renewal;
- cash state where supported;
- liabilities/obligations where supported.

Unknown remains unknown.

Do not substitute accounting exports for bank/payment truth.

Create economics views by:
- offer;
- customer/account;
- vertical;
- channel;
- provider;
- model;
- partner;
- experiment;
- cohort.

Long-term allocator should move attention/capital toward verified contribution and away from vanity success.

# L. PROVIDER MARKET / ROUTER

Generalize evidence-aware routing beyond LLMs.

For each provider class maintain:
- capability;
- price/cost unit;
- latency;
- reliability;
- region;
- data policy;
- rate limits;
- quality evidence;
- outage state;
- test/live mode;
- auth readiness;
- idempotency;
- reconciliation;
- fallback compatibility.

Provider categories:
- LLMs;
- web/search;
- browser;
- email;
- SMS;
- voice;
- CRM;
- calendar;
- invoicing/payment;
- signatures;
- forms;
- storage/database;
- analytics;
- content/social;
- deployment/cloud.

Selection must respect authority/budget/privacy/data residency before economics.

# M. EXPERIMENTATION ENGINE

Every meaningful commercial hypothesis should be expressible as a bounded experiment:

- hypothesis;
- treatment/control where feasible;
- target population;
- channel;
- offer;
- sample/stop constraints;
- economic downside ceiling;
- founder-minute ceiling;
- success evidence;
- failure evidence;
- observation period;
- conclusion state.

Avoid fake statistical sophistication on tiny samples.

Prefer cheap falsification before expensive build.

One active first-money experiment by default. Portfolio research can continue offline.

# N. KNOWLEDGE / MEMORY / BRAIN V3

Make UberBond survive model/chat turnover permanently.

Brain should provide:
- one-command bootstrap;
- canonical source graph;
- current handoff;
- historical initiatives;
- decisions;
- contradictions;
- supersessions;
- active programs;
- capability registry;
- provider registry;
- offer registry;
- experiment registry;
- external proof frontier;
- owner actions;
- test/deployment receipts;
- unresolved memories;
- source provenance.

Chat/share URLs are provenance pointers until imported.

Build incremental import from accessible chat/export transcripts into durable structured records with dedupe/supersession.

No future agent should require the founder to narrate UberBond from scratch.

# O. FOUNDER COMMAND CENTER

Create a ruthless exception-only operating surface.

Founder should see:
- cleared/reversed/disputed money;
- active experiments and their real economics;
- serious customer exceptions;
- system health;
- provider outages;
- high-impact approvals;
- legal/tax/KYC/credential boundaries;
- capital decisions;
- at most three owner actions.

Do not make the founder inspect queues, logs, research dumps or routine tasks.

Every owner action must include:
- exact action;
- why software cannot do it;
- location/screen/provider;
- minutes;
- cost;
- evidence of completion;
- what it unlocks;
- safe default if ignored.

# P. SELF-BUILDING SOFTWARE FACTORY

Within bounded authority, UberBond should be able to improve its own repository.

Required pipeline:

`observed gap -> evidence -> expected leverage -> code/design candidate -> branch -> implementation -> tests -> mutation -> security review -> independent review -> preview -> merge -> deploy -> post-deploy observation -> learning`

Add automatic stopping when:
- confidence too low;
- safety-sensitive;
- authority change;
- migration risk high;
- test evidence unavailable;
- provider spend required;
- user/customer consequence possible.

Self-improvement proposals cannot grant themselves additional authority.

# Q. RELIABILITY / CHAOS / RECOVERY

Attack production-oriented invariants systematically:
- duplicate scheduler delivery;
- crash before/after durable receipt;
- Postgres disconnect;
- partial transaction;
- provider timeout;
- provider succeeded but response lost;
- retries;
- dead letters;
- worker crash;
- deployment during occurrence;
- policy/source drift;
- clock skew;
- stale evidence;
- replay after upgrade;
- outage/fallback;
- concurrency;
- malformed external payload;
- poison task;
- high-volume queue;
- cost exhaustion.

Build recovery receipts and ensure ambiguous external state blocks blind repetition.

# R. SECURITY / PRIVACY / TENANCY

The wealth engine must not become a data-leak engine.

Enforce:
- tenant boundaries;
- least authority;
- secret scanning;
- credential non-persistence;
- PII minimization;
- public/private source distinction;
- data-retention rules;
- deletion/suppression;
- SSRF defenses;
- URL policy;
- redirect policy;
- prompt-injection containment;
- tool-call authorization;
- output sanitization;
- audit events;
- log redaction;
- webhook signature verification;
- replay protection.

# S. CLOUD / GLOBAL OPERABILITY

Architect for global operability without premature infrastructure complexity.

Verify/configure:
- stateless web/runtime boundaries;
- durable Postgres truth;
- deployment identity;
- provider-neutral integrations;
- timezones/local business hours;
- currency as data, no implicit FX;
- locale/language support;
- Arabic/English where relevant;
- regional/provider constraints;
- retries and rate limits;
- portability/backup/export;
- health and rollback.

Do not claim global legal availability merely because code can run globally.

# T. FIRST REALITY ACTIVATION LADDER

After the internal system is strong, make external blockers painfully concrete.

Activation ladder:

1. production web/control plane current;
2. production scheduled zero-provider cycles;
3. provider test-mode adapters;
4. one lawful distribution lane configured;
5. one payment collection route confirmed;
6. one commercial canary activated with explicit owner authorization;
7. first real interested buyer;
8. first cleared payment;
9. first accepted delivery;
10. first renewal/second cleared payment;
11. repeated positive contribution;
12. founder-absence wall-clock proof;
13. partner/multi-channel replication.

Software work must not pretend to complete stages 7–13.

# U. REPOSITORY CONSOLIDATION

Reduce founder/agent confusion.

By mission end, current main should have:
- one canonical brain;
- one scheduler/autonomy spine;
- one economic truth hierarchy;
- one opportunity registry;
- one offer registry/compiler;
- one capability registry;
- one distribution registry/allocator;
- one account/sales timeline;
- one payment/commercial truth layer;
- one delivery/acceptance truth layer;
- one provider registry/router;
- one test/release gate;
- one current handoff.

Legacy modules may exist, but canonical ownership must be explicit.

# V. MERGE LAW

The owner wants the useful system merged, not a museum of draft branches.

For every PR:
- rebase/reconcile current main;
- verify dependency status;
- run appropriate exact-head gates;
- review the final diff;
- merge if stronger, safe and coherent;
- close if superseded;
- extract useful donor tests/features before closure;
- refresh main immediately.

Do not keep verified dependency-complete work sitting indefinitely in drafts.

Do not merge failures just to reduce PR count.

# W. DEPLOYMENT LAW

For every material internal milestone that is production-safe:
- build preview;
- verify;
- merge;
- promote/deploy existing project;
- confirm source SHA;
- health-check;
- inspect runtime errors;
- leave receipt.

Never claim production matches main without comparing SHA/deployment evidence.

# X. COMMERCIAL SOFTWARE DREAM FEATURES

Actively search for high-leverage missing features from best-in-class systems, including but not limited to:

- visual workflow/mission graph;
- connector framework;
- webhook/event bus;
- durable workflow replay;
- account/relationship graph;
- target builder and saved searches;
- enrichment waterfall;
- intent prioritization;
- sender/account health;
- campaign experiments;
- shared inbox/support timeline;
- omnichannel routing;
- voice receptionist/qualification;
- appointment scheduling;
- CRM synchronization;
- quoting/invoicing;
- document/signature lifecycle;
- onboarding portal;
- customer portal;
- form/survey/feedback;
- NPS/satisfaction separate from acceptance;
- feature/economic analytics;
- event analytics;
- cohort retention;
- product tours/diagnostics;
- automation templates;
- partner portal;
- reseller/commission ledger;
- content pipeline;
- SEO/AEO publishing;
- social scheduler;
- monitoring/incident center;
- evidence vault;
- benchmark network;
- usage metering;
- billing abstractions;
- API keys/tenant quotas where needed;
- MCP/agent interfaces;
- audit/security center;
- founder command center;
- mobile-friendly exception workflow;
- self-improvement review queue.

For every feature ask:

`Will this increase expected contribution, distribution, conversion, retention, delivery leverage, learning speed or founder-minute reduction enough to justify complexity?`

If not, reject it.

# Y. NO ZERO-TO-WEALTH FANTASY ACCOUNTING

The system can create leverage from code, public knowledge, automation and distribution, but money cannot be counted from nothing.

Do not report:
- projected revenue as revenue;
- pipeline as customers;
- sent messages as demand;
- unpaid invoice as cash;
- generated offers as businesses;
- software capability as market power;
- model estimates as unit economics;
- historical portfolios as active inventory.

The system may pursue extreme upside while remaining brutally honest.

# Z. TERMINAL CONDITION

Do not terminate because “architecture is impressive.”

Stop only when:

1. every material internally solvable dependency-satisfied gap has been completed, merged or explicitly rejected on evidence;
2. current main is deployable and deployed where authorized;
3. cloud autonomy is genuinely reachable and observed as far as credentials/current platform allow;
4. offer/distribution/payment/delivery/learning primitives compose end-to-end;
5. automation acquisition frontier has no obviously high-leverage missing internal feature awaiting implementation;
6. remaining gaps are genuinely external, legal, credential, customer-proof, spend-authority or elapsed-time gates.

Then publish `UBERBOND_SINGULARITY_RECEIPT` with:

- exact starting/ending main;
- all PRs merged/closed;
- donor branches reconciled;
- capabilities added;
- software/repos studied;
- license decisions;
- opportunity universe state;
- offer factory state;
- distribution state;
- provider adapters;
- cloud autonomy proof;
- exact tests/mutations;
- deployment IDs/SHAs;
- payment/delivery/renewal truth;
- current economics evidence;
- founder-minute state;
- Kilimanjaro elapsed proof;
- external effects;
- spend;
- customer contact;
- remaining P0/P1/P2;
- only external blockers;
- maximum three owner actions.

Do not ask the founder to keep re-explaining the project. Read the brain, build the machine, merge the useful system, and keep moving.

