Therefore #181 remains intentionally unmerged. Its next promotion gate is still trustworthy exact-head execution of the three focused suites plus review against current main. Do not substitute Vercel buildability for semantic test proof.

External effects this reconciliation: 0 customer/prospect contact, 0 provider/model calls, $0 spend, 0 DNS/credential/KYC/payment changes, 0 money movement, 0 customer/production-data mutation. The only production effect was the authorized Git-linked deployment automatically created by merging #182.

Promotion review on exact head `1a0da9674c7d99f33436639364893fd65af2d72b`:

- independently reviewed full two-file diff; no `lite/` changes and no new provider/network/external-effect call path;
- branch remains 0 behind exact base `59ad681a1b1b192953d6245c9b0f87055835ceff` and GitHub reports it mergeable;
- exact-head Vercel deployment `dpl_6AyjAtevgNE52QWe2XjqytvFvf4h` is READY and metadata binds it to this exact SHA/branch/PR;
- build log explicitly cloned commit `1a0da96`, ran `vercel build`, completed the Node build using `server.mjs`, deployed outputs and completed successfully;
- GitHub Actions run `33233003825` is runner/account infrastructure non-evidence: postgres, deterministic and browser jobs all ended with no executed steps. It is not represented as a source pass or source failure;
- the 7 focused semantic tests are committed but were not executable from the current local runtime because github.com DNS resolution remains unavailable. No test-pass claim is made.

The runtime delta is fail-closed and narrows the existing scheduled TaskIntent path: canonical autonomy relay compilation now composes through the already-merged employee role contract/relay, keeps `LOCAL_PREPARATION`, max external cost 0, and all existing autonomy forbidden actions. Worker-side role enforcement from #185 remains a second independent gate.

External-effect ledger: customer/prospect contact 0; outbound messages 0; model/provider executions 0; spend $0; DNS/credential/KYC/payment changes 0; money movement 0; customer/production-data mutations 0. The Vercel preview was created by existing Git integration. No commercial truth was changed.

This is complementary to what just landed in #212, not a duplicate — but as drafted it reopens the hole #212 closed, and the two need to be reconciled before this merges.

**Different halves of the same seam.** #211 enforces the *bound* direction at the relay entry point: a role-bound task's result and receipt must match before replay, lease acceptance or terminal mutation. That is real and it is not what #212 did. #212 closed the *unbound* direction inside `employeeRoleIdentityErrors`, which used to return `[]` whenever the task carried no binding — so a generic task accepted a result self-asserting `employee:executive/cfo`, and the claim was carried into the durable submission payload.

**The interaction.** `validateEmployeeRoleRelayResultAdmission` returns early on the unbound path without calling `employeeRoleIdentityErrors` at all:

